## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to influence without authority, map stakeholders, and drive governance in a multi-team cloud/data environment.

## Key Concepts
- Influence without authority
- Data contracts and versioning
- Pilot, feature flags, and phased rollout
- Metrics: ETL errors, latency, data quality
- Governance and follow-up

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple versioned event parser
function parseEvent(event) {
  const v = event.version || 1;
  if (v === 1) {
    return { userId: event.uid, action: event.act };
  } else if (v === 2) {
    return { userId: event.user_id, action: event.action, meta: event.meta };
  }
  return null;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What metrics would you track to prove the initiative's value?
- How would you handle resistance from teams wary of changing schemas?

## Why This Is Asked

Gauges practical conflict handling, clarity in decision criteria, and discipline in following up with measurable feedback loops.

## Key Concepts

- Surface interests, separate people from problem
- Generate multiple actionable options
- Use objective criteria to decide
- Establish concrete feedback loops and ownership

## Code Example

```javascript
function scoreOption(option) {
  const criteria = { risk: 3, impact: 3, maintenance: 2, time: 2 };
  return Object.keys(criteria).reduce((acc, k) => {
    return acc + (option[k] ? criteria[k] : -criteria[k]);
  }, 0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you document the decision so future audits understand it?
- What indicators would trigger a re-evaluation of the chosen option?

